---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { PROFILE, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/me.png';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`About | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
                        description="About Samuel Cheston: an independent developer building authentication systems, game infrastructure, and the games and tools around them."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main" class="shell about-main">
                        <a class="back-link" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Back to the portfolio</a>
			<div class="about-heading">
                                <h1>Curious about<br /><em>how it all connects.</em></h1>
                                <p>I build across the stack because the ideas I want to explore don't stop at one layer.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="about-grid">
				<aside class="about-facts" aria-label="At a glance">
					<Image
						class="about-portrait"
						src={portrait}
						alt="Portrait of Samuel Cheston"
						width={96}
						height={96}
						widths={[96, 192]}
						sizes="96px"
						format="webp"
						fit="cover"
					/>
					<dl>
						<div><dt>Who</dt><dd>Samuel Cheston</dd></div>
						<div><dt>How I work</dt><dd>Independent developer</dd></div>
                                                <div><dt>Interests</dt><dd>Systems, games, and tools</dd></div>
					</dl>
                                        <a class="arrow-link" href={PROFILE.github}>GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
				</aside>
				<div class="about-story">
					<section aria-labelledby="starting-point">
                                                <h2 id="starting-point">One idea leads to another.</h2>
                                                <p>MatchCore started with an idea: bring Elo-based matchmaking to Minecraft. Exploring that idea led to the services, interfaces, and tools needed to connect the wider experience.</p>
                                                <p>I independently develop these projects, from the underlying services to the interfaces around them. HRPAuth is one part of that larger effort.</p>
					</section>
					<section aria-labelledby="foundation">
                                                <h2 id="foundation">Think in connections.</h2>
                                                <p>I'm interested in how software fits together: authentication and game clients, protocols and services, infrastructure and the interfaces people use.</p>
                                                <p>HRPAuth explores those connections through a shared identity core and an ecosystem of services. Elsewhere, Silo40 explores configurable simulation, and Avalon explores game networking.</p>
					</section>
					<section aria-labelledby="beyond">
                                                <h2 id="beyond">A note on attribution.</h2>
                                                <p>The work here is independently developed. Some projects integrate with existing open-source software, and some reuse my own earlier work. The project directory groups them into series, so those relationships stay visible.</p>
						<div class="about-actions">
                                                        <a class="button button-dark" href="/projects">Explore the projects <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                                                        <a class="arrow-link" href="/#connect">Connect <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
						</div>
					</section>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
